## Phase 2: Execution Path

### Upgrading from SuiteCRM 8.x

SuiteCRM 8 upgrades are executed entirely via the Command Line Interface (CLI).

1. #### Download the target version package:
   Grab the production-ready installable `.zip` file from the official SuiteCRM release page. https://suitecrm.com/releases/
   ```
   cd /var/www/suitecrm/tmp/package/upgrade
   sudo -u www-data wget https://suitecrm.com/download/168/suite810/568626/suitecrm-8-10-1.zip
   ```

1. #### Set permission
   Execute the migration script using the exact name of the downloaded package.
   ```
   # 1. Navigate to the root directory (just to be certain)
   cd /var/www/suitecrm

   # 2. Change ownership of EVERYTHING to the web server user
   sudo chown -R www-data:www-data .

   # 3. Set standard directories to 755 (Directories need executable rights to be traversed)
   sudo find . -type d -exec chmod 755 {} \;

   # 4. Set standard files to 644 (Read/Write for owner, Read for others)
   sudo find . -type f -exec chmod 644 {} \;

   # 5. Set higher permissions on writable directories required by SuiteCRM
   # (This includes the legacy core folders inside the SuiteCRM 8 structure)
   sudo chmod -R 775 cache custom modules themes upload public/legacy/cache public/legacy/custom public/legacy/modules public/legacy/themes public/legacy/upload

   # 6. Set higher permissions on the config files so the installer can update them
   sudo chmod 664 config.php public/legacy/config.php public/legacy/config_override.php 2>/dev/null || true

   chmod 775 ./bin/console 
   ```


1. #### Run the Core Upgrade command:
   Execute the migration script using the exact name of the downloaded package.
   ```
   cd /var/www/suitecrm
   sudo -u www-data ./bin/console suitecrm:app:upgrade -t "suitecrm-8-10-1"
   ```

1. #### Run the Finalize command:
   Once the core update finishes, finalize the asset generation and database schema changes.
   ```bash
    sudo -u www-data ./bin/console suitecrm:app:upgrade-finalize -t "SuiteCRM-8.10.1"
   ```








